  <h1>Exercise: Move for a Better You</h1>

  <h3>1. Why Exercise is Non-Negotiable</h3>
  <p>Exercise is not punishment; it’s self-care in motion. It boosts not only physical health but also mental resilience.</p>

  <h3>2. Physical Benefits</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Improves cardiovascular health</li>
    <li>Builds muscle and bone strength</li>
    <li>Boosts metabolism and endurance</li>
    <li>Regulates hormones and mood</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>3. Mental Benefits</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Reduces anxiety and depression</li>
    <li>Improves memory and cognitive function</li>
    <li>Increases self-esteem</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4. Simple Workout Routine for Beginners</h3>
  <table border="1" cellpadding="8" style="border-collapse:collapse;">
    <tr><th>Day</th><th>Focus</th><th>Workout Type</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Mon</td><td>Full Body</td><td>Bodyweight workout</td><td>30 min</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Tue</td><td>Cardio</td><td>Brisk walking/jogging</td><td>20–30 min</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Wed</td><td>Strength</td><td>Dumbbell/resistance bands</td><td>30 min</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Thu</td><td>Yoga</td><td>Flexibility & breathing</td><td>25 min</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Fri</td><td>HIIT</td><td>High-intensity circuit</td><td>20 min</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sat</td><td>Fun</td><td>Dance, sports, cycling</td><td>30+ min</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sun</td><td>Rest</td><td>Meditation & stretching</td><td>15 min</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h3>5. Fitness Motivation Tips</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Set realistic goals (like “3 workouts/week”)</li>
    <li>Track progress visually (journal or app)</li>
    <li>Reward yourself for consistency</li>
    <li>Workout with friends or music</li>
  </ul>
</div>
